/* A designed loss (wave 6), composed onto ScreenScaffold. bible 4.11 makes
 * this a TEACHING screen, not a failure screen: the diagnosis is the content
 * and the Pale grant is the recovery, so only the headline is coral.
 *
 * THIRTY-ONE DECLARATIONS BECAME TEN IN PHASE 8 TASK 11 AND NONE OF THE
 * TWENTY-ONE WAS REPLACED BY A COPY HERE, which is the test of whether a
 * screen composes the layer or re-derives it:
 *   - the root's `padding: var(--gutter)` and `align-items: center` are the
 *     scaffold's content region, which puts the gutter on
 *     `unity-scroll-view__content-container` so an elevated card's shadow is
 *     not clipped at the viewport edge.
 *   - `__headline`'s size, weight and ink are `.t-hero` and `.t-danger`.
 *     Both are single-class selectors in Theme.uss and `.t-danger` is
 *     declared after `.t-hero`, so the coral wins the colour and the 28px
 *     survives.
 *   - `__diagnosis`'s --surface fill, --radius-card, 1px --divider border and
 *     --space-4 of padding were SectionCard's surface written out again,
 *     minus the elevation - five declarations against a component that
 *     already carried all five and a drop shadow. Its --text-card-title is
 *     `.t-card-title` and its --ink is that class's too.
 *   - `__granted`'s size, weight and ink are `.t-secondary` and `.t-success`.
 *   - `__grants`'s --green-tint fill, row radius, 12px padding and
 *     `width: 100%` are gone and nothing took their place: that panel drew a
 *     full-width green block behind a single 160px card, and the whole block
 *     drew blank on a defeat with no resupply. WaveDefeatView.Bind has it.
 *   - `__grant`'s size, ink and wrap were describing a Label that has not
 *     been in this tree since the grants became CreatureCards. The rule
 *     survives as the one line the card grid does need, which is the gap
 *     under a wrapped row.
 *   - `__retry`'s top margin and full width are the CTA row's own padding and
 *     its `flex-direction: column`, and the button's whole treatment is
 *     Theme's `.btn-primary`.
 */
.wave-defeat-view { flex-grow: 1; }


/* Sentences, not labels, so they wrap. The headline runs to three lines at
 * 28px on a 430 frame with the wave-6 breach in it, and the diagnosis is the
 * longest single sentence in the app. */
/* CENTRED AS TEXT, NOT AS LAYOUT. This screen's root used to carry
 * `align-items: center` and it was dropped on the claim that the scaffold's
 * content region supplies it. It does not - `.screen-scaffold__content` is
 * `flex-grow` alone and its content-container rule sets padding only - so a
 * short verdict stretched to full content width and rendered flush left,
 * while SpliceRevealView, the third screen of the same beat, stayed centred.
 *
 * The fix is text-align rather than the container's `align-items`, because
 * this is a Label whose TEXT is off-centre, not a box in the wrong place.
 * Centring the content container instead makes every sibling shrink-wrap,
 * which collapses the stat row into overlapping cells - measured, in a
 * capture, before this was written. */
.wave-defeat-view__headline {
    white-space: normal;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
}

.wave-defeat-view__diagnosis { white-space: normal; }

.wave-defeat-view__resupply { flex-direction: column; }

/* Sits directly over the cards it introduces, so it reads as their caption
 * rather than as a line of its own. */
.wave-defeat-view__granted { margin-bottom: var(--space-1); }

/* The resupply, laid out like RosterView's grid and for the same reason: a
 * CreatureCard is a fixed 160px, two of them plus the 12px gutter leave 406
 * of space for 320 of card, and `space-between` is what puts a pair against
 * both edges and an odd third at the left where the next row starts. */
.wave-defeat-view__grants {
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
}

.wave-defeat-view__grant { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
